# A stand-in for a shared figure style, used only by tests/test_figstyle.py.
# Every value is far from matplotlib's default so that a test can tell the style from the defaults.
# Colours in a cycler are written without '#', which would start a comment here.
font.family: monospace
font.size: 17
axes.labelsize: 19
xtick.labelsize: 15
ytick.labelsize: 15
axes.linewidth: 2.5
axes.prop_cycle: cycler('color', ['ff00ff', '00ffff', 'ffff00'])
# The spine keys are deliberately absent: since 2026-11-13 `figures.figure` hides the top and right spines itself, so a style
# cannot restore them and they would prove nothing about what a style reaches. `axes.linewidth` is what proves it for the axes.
